# Rust build artefacts
/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# Auxiliary crates (fuzz/, ct-tests/) keep their lockfiles untracked: their
# manifests deliberately float (`version = "0.2"`, not a pin) so resolution
# stays aligned with the workspace's own graph.
Cargo.lock
# The workspace lockfile IS tracked. flake.nix's packages.default reads it
# (cargoLock.lockFile = ./Cargo.lock), so without it `nix build` fails on a
# clean checkout; it also makes CI advisory scans reproducible instead of
# re-resolving on every run. Committing a lockfile does not constrain
# downstream consumers of these library crates.
!/Cargo.lock

